Description: Restore the requested font family after fontconfig config substitution
 Fontconfig configuration can prepend families ahead of the one that was
 requested. conf.d/48-spacing.conf (before fontconfig 2.18.2 - e.g. Debian 13
 ships 2.15) prepends the generic family "monospace" whenever the pattern
 carries spacing=mono. Family rules that then match that injected
 "monospace" - e.g. Debian/Ubuntu's fonts-noto-cjk 70-fonts-noto-cjk.conf -
 prepend a CJK font with binding="strong" for lang=zh-cn/zh-tw/zh-hk.
 Fontconfig then prefers those over the font the user configured, so with
 LANG=zh_CN.UTF-8 ghostty ignores font-family entirely: every cell is sized
 from Noto Sans Mono CJK (text looks cramped) and `ghostty +show-face
 --string=M` reports the CJK font.
 .
 Reproducible without ghostty (spacing=100 is the hint ghostty adds):
   $ fc-match 'JetBrainsMono Nerd Font Mono:spacing=100:lang=zh-cn'
   Noto Sans Mono CJK SC
   $ fc-match 'JetBrainsMono Nerd Font Mono:lang=zh-cn'
   JetBrainsMono Nerd Font Mono
 .
 Ghostty adds the spacing hint to every pattern so that generic searches prefer
 monospace faces (that is what the ghostty#1984 fix relies on), so rather than
 dropping the hint we put the requested family back at the front of the family
 list after substitution and keep the substituted families as fallbacks. This
 matches what fontconfig >= 2.18.2 does itself (it adds to "genericfamily"
 instead of "family" for spacing=mono).
 .
 Measured on Debian 13 / fontconfig 2.15.0 (zh_CN.UTF-8):
   * configured family exists  -> that family (before: Noto Sans Mono CJK SC)
   * configured family missing -> still a monospace fallback, as ghostty#1984
     intends (before, with the hint dropped, it regresses to a proportional font)
Origin: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/fontconfig/fontconfig/-/work_items/539
Bug: https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/fontconfig/fontconfig/-/commit/1ed41a70 (fixed in fontconfig 2.18.2)
Forwarded: no (downstream workaround; upstream report: ghostty discussion #9667)
  The fontconfig fix is not in any Debian/Ubuntu release yet: Debian 13
  (trixie) 2.15.0, Debian sid/forky 2.17.1, Ubuntu 24.04 LTS 2.15.0 and
  Ubuntu 26.04 LTS 2.17.1 all still prepend to "family".
Last-Update: 2026-11-09
